On Mon, Jul 18, 2005 at 09:25:21AM +0200, Mark Ter Morshuizen wrote:
> 
> Can anyone tell me if there is a difference between the B3107-CA and
> B3007-CA CPU boards? I have a B3107-CA in my 5300 and can get a
> B3007-CA as a second CPU. Will this work?

Yes, it should.

According to my sources, the only difference is the part numbers, one
indicating UNIX/VMX (B3007) and one indicating NT (B3107).

HOWEVER, the suffix (-CA) MUST BE THE SAME!!!!

This is an indicator of the speed (in this case, 533MHz), and different
speeds CANNOT BE MIXED in a system.

Good luck.

