I have got my recently upgraded Debian/Sarge on two alphas, both running
2.4.31 fine.

I am trying to boot one of the machines (a PC164) under 2.6.12.3 under
SRM.  It gets part way through the boot process having recognized the
scsi drives, etc.  However, it hits a kernel panic which appears to be
related to a warning just before that it cannot find the console.  I
have the console set to vga, but it apparently is not enough.  Is there
something special for alphas and the console to get this new kernel
running ?  I am including my .config here.

