I have got my recently upgraded Debian/Sarge on two alphas, both running 2.4.31 fine.<BR>
<BR>
I am trying to boot one of the machines (a PC164) under 2.6.12.3 under SRM.&nbsp; It gets part way through the boot process having recognized the scsi drives, etc.&nbsp; However, it hits a kernel panic which appears to be related to a warning just before that it cannot find the console.&nbsp; I have the console set to vga, but it apparently is not enough.&nbsp; Is there something special for alphas and the console to get this new kernel running ?&nbsp; I am including my .config here.<BR>
