-------- Original Message --------
Subject: 	[gentoo-alpha] MILO and Adaptec AHA2940AU
Date: 	Thu, 21 Jul 2005 21:33:54 -0400
From: 	Jean-S=E9bastien Guay <jean_seb@videotron.ca>
Reply-To: 	gentoo-alpha@lists.gentoo.org
To: 	Gentoo-Alpha Mailing List <gentoo-alpha@lists.gentoo.org>



Hello everyone,

I have a hardware-related question for you guys and gals today. I want=20
to install a new HDD in my Alpha XL-366 (XLT system type,=20
AlphaBIOS-only, so I'm stuck with MILO...). Now, the first problem is=20
that I can't run it off the onboard sym53c810 SCSI controller, because=20
(as I understand it) it is a Wide SCSI-2 device, and the sym53c810 only=20
supports Fast SCSI-2, and the problem is that the kernel driver tries to=20
set the controller to Wide which causes errors to be continuously=20
printed to the console.

(See=20
http://www.mail-archive.com/debian-alpha@lists.debian.org/msg22571.html=20
for a description of the exact same problem. That person solved it by=20
patching the kernel driver to turn off Wide mode, which is a bit drastic=20
and I don't want to do it each time I build my kernel...)

So what I'm trying now is to run the drive off an Adaptec AHA2940AU=20
controller I had in another unused machine. The controller and drive are=20
detected on bootup, I see them in the BIOS, so all seems peachy. But=20
when MILO starts up and tries to detect the machine's devices (after=20
typing in a "boot" command, or when doing an "ls" for example), it hangs=20
right after detecting the Adaptec controller.

See https://www.redhat.com/archives/axp-list/2002-August/msg00185.html=20
(first 1/3 of the message), where the same problem is described.

First question is why does MILO 2.2-18 hang when loading the Adaptec=20
driver? Is it a known bug with this hardware/software combination?

That person says that downgrading to MILO 2.2-17 allowed him to boot.=20
When I try that version, it hangs at "Swapping to PALcode at=20
0x80080000". I even tried linload.exe version 1.3a and 1.5, both give=20
the same problem. How do I get MILO 2.2-17 to boot?

Of course, if someone could tell me how to disable Wide mode in my=20
2.6.11.8 kernel's sym53c8xx driver without having to hack the code at=20
each kernel upgrade, that would (probably) solve the root problem and=20
eliminate the need for the Adaptec controller. I saw that passing=20
'sym53c8xx=3D"wide:0"' to the kernel in the boot command would do the=20
trick, if the sym53c8xx driver were built as a module. But the=20
controller is needed to boot at all, so I have to compile it into the=20
kernel or else the kernel starts but doesn't see the root device, and=20
with the driver compiled into the kernel it doesn't check those=20
arguments (argh). One solution could be to install an IDE controller=20
with a small IDE drive to boot from, and then compile the sym53c8xx=20
driver as a module, but I'd like to keep that as a last resort and try=20
to make it work with what I have first.

I anxiously await any suggestions. Thanks in advance,

J-S

